    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>640</x>
      <y>4700</y>
      <w>480</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Host, Refreshable, Paged, Pages, RoundButton, NavButton,
RoundedCard and GradientPanel are nested types of Ui.
Ui itself is a static helper class (colours, fonts, builders,
table styling, icons) used by every screen.
bg=#FFFBE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2300</x>
      <y>4150</y>
      <w>470</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>OperatorPanel creates two Backend objects, one for
members and one for providers. They forward to
MemberController and ProviderController, so the
rules stay in the controllers.
bg=#FFFBE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>60</x>
      <y>4550</y>
      <w>420</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Every screen calls the core classes of diagram 1.
No screen reads or writes a data file itself:
ChocAnDatabase does that.
bg=#FFFBE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes></additional_attributes>
